<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction (Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator))",
        "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction faithfully reproduces Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-3> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 91.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit-v2) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py> ;
    schema:about "Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2 or 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability",
        "reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction",
        "reported_in_source: Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA",
        "transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM periodicity" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "3. Phase/Delay Oscillators" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "I. Enaima (Vertebrata)" ;
    pk:aristotelianPoionForm "Periodic Somites & Segments" ;
    pk:aristotelianPosonLaw "Somite Length S = u·T_clock" ;
    pk:aristotelianSubalternClass "Mammalia (Zootoka)" ;
    pk:biologicalGenus "Mus" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/317bc3c/2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py; output: docs/media/yap_excitable_segmentation_comparison.png; organism: Mus musculus (mouse E9.5-E10.5 presomitic mesoderm LuVeLu Lfng-Venus / Hes7 excitable oscillator); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: cd7e22124efc1260387a25c216bb931744f6e84e2199a778a5e3eb6d86c4980d; artifact_sha256: a3efccf96655e7782baf380b4a0a322aa410d13fbeb60929144cf4b0d65fa1fb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/scout_manifest.json=852a6ed7852f291d..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json=629b1b5e9d80a634...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction | Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109) | RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability | 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010); transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM periodicity; does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2 or 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy]" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/S0006-3495(61)86902-6>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2017.08.043>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature10137>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature11804> ;
    pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-code-traceability>,
