<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction — Model fidelity to source: 94/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Faithfully implements Hubaud et al.'s (2017) FitzHugh-Nagumo cubic fast-slow ODE/PDE `tau_u du/dt = u - u^3/3 - v + I_eff(Y_nuc, J_Dll1) + D_u nabla^2 u`, `tau_v dv/dt = u + a - b v` with exact cubic root continuation, Jacobian trace/determinant Hopf stability analysis (`|u_H| = sqrt(1 - epsilon*b) = 0.9675`), suprathreshold single-spike excitability, and 2D diffusive target-wave propagation (L120-520), verified by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys) in `morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean`." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.4e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Extracts 5 reference-anchored quantitative morphometric measurements via `measure_morphoeval()` (L600-665): FHN supercritical Hopf threshold `|u_H| = 0.9675` (cubic knee barrier `4/3 = 1.3333`), critical nuclear YAP threshold `Y_nuc_crit = 0.6109`, Latrunculin A-rescued autonomous oscillation period `T_osc = 141.50 min` vs empirical `142.0 min`, 6-regime oscillating cell fraction Pearson `r = 0.9976` (`p = 8.43e-06`, `RMSE = 0.0469`), and bilateral SEM specimen somite spacing `47.14 +/- 9.48 px` (`CV = 0.2010`)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-6-regime-yap-notch-perturbation-oscillating-cell-fraction-pearson-correlation-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-critical-nuclear-yap-excitability-threshold-y-nuc-crit-at-j-dll1-0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-fitzhugh-nagumo-supercritical-hopf-bifurcation-threshold-u-h>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-latrunculin-a-yap-inhibited-autonomous-oscillation-period-t-osc>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-measurement-vertebrate-somite-psm-specimen-bilateral-somite-spacing-s-obs>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 9.2e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquié (2017) excitable FitzHugh-Nagumo segmentation clock gated by YAP mechanotransduction — MorphoEval overall 91.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 post-remediation evaluation of `2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py` (91.7/100, up from 60.6/100 in Pass 1; +31.1 overall). The remediated script implements the full FitzHugh-Nagumo fast-slow excitable segmentation-clock model gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction (`I_eff = I_basal + J_Dll1 - gamma_YAP * Y_nuc`), solves exact cubic nullcline intersections and supercritical Hopf bifurcation thresholds (`|u_H| = 0.9675`, `Y_nuc_crit = 0.6109`, cubic knee barrier `4/3 = 1.3333`), reproduces all 6 experimental perturbation regimes from Hubaud et al. (2017) (isolated fibronectin quiescent, Dll1-coated, Latrunculin A F-actin inhibition rescue at `T_osc = 141.50 min`, Y-27632 Rockout rescue, intact high-density mPSM, and constitutively active `Yap5SA` arrest; oscillating fraction Pearson `r = 0.9976`, `RMSE = 0.0469`), demonstrates suprathreshold single-pulse excitability, solves the 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE (`wave_contrast = 0.931` vs `0.0144` under `Yap5SA` block), and segments the vendored vertebrate somite/PSM SEM specimen (`mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg`, bilateral spacing `47.14 px`, `CV = 0.2010`), backed by 3 machine-checked Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_027_yap_excitable_segmentation.lean`. Overall 91.5/100 (faithfulness 91.5, reproducibility 91.7); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 317bc3c; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 94, Morphological realism / specimen match 89, Parameter expressivity 92, Morphometric validation 92, Source and data traceability 93, Code-to-model traceability 91, Reproducibility package 91. Output judged: docs/media/yap_excitable_segmentation_comparison.png: rendered output of 2016-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation.py at 317bc3c, image/png, 1162113 B, 2775×1650 px, artifact_sha256 a3efccf96655e7782baf380b4a0a322aa410d13fbeb60929144cf4b0d65fa1fb (sha256 a3efccf96655e7782baf380b4a0a322aa410d13fbeb60929144cf4b0d65fa1fb), spec_fingerprint cd7e22124efc1260387a25c216bb931744f6e84e2199a778a5e3eb6d86c4980d. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: cd7e22124efc1260387a25c216bb931744f6e84e2199a778a5e3eb6d86c4980d; artifact_sha256: a3efccf96655e7782baf380b4a0a322aa410d13fbeb60929144cf4b0d65fa1fb; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg=8b80971796cb29e2..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/scout_manifest.json=852a6ed7852f291d..., datasets/yap_excitable_segmentation/yap_excitable_segmentation_reference.json=629b1b5e9d80a634...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-yap-excitable-segmentation-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Hubaud, Regev, Mahadevan & Pourquie (2017) Cell 171:668-682 FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable oscillator model of primary mouse presomitic mesoderm (PSM) cells gated by nuclear YAP mechanotransduction | Quiescent excitable state in isolated spread fibronectin PSM cells (high nuclear YAP) rescued into ~140 min autonomous LuVeLu oscillations by Latrunculin A, Y-27632 (Rockout), or Yap1 inhibition, and blocked by constitutively active Yap5SA; reconstructed_in_script: Analytical cubic nullcline continuation, Jacobian spectrum, and supercritical Hopf bifurcation diagram across Y_nuc in [0, 1] (|u_H| = 0.9675, Y_crit = 0.6109) | RK4 single-cell & ensemble simulations across all 6 Hubaud et al. (2017) perturbation regimes (Pearson r = 0.9976, RMSE = 0.0469) plus subthreshold vs suprathreshold single-pulse excitability | 2D reaction-diffusion mPSM target-wave PDE solver with Yap5SA constitutive block control and bilateral somite DoG peak segmentation on mouse_psm_somites_specimen.jpg (47.14 px mean spacing, CV = 0.2010); transfer_boundary: Fast-slow 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo phenomenological reduction of the Notch/FGF/Wnt/YAP mouse PSM segmentation clock compared with dorsal vertebrate paraxial somite SEM periodicity; does_not_claim: Explicit molecular transcriptional-translational delay equations for Hes7/Lfng/Axin2 or 3D focal-adhesion traction force microscopy." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Couple the 2-variable FitzHugh-Nagumo excitable core to an explicit spatial FGF/Wnt gradient decay along the anteroposterior axis to model wavefront arrest of excitable waves into discrete somite clefts.",
        "remediation needed: Incorporate explicit substrate-stiffness traction mechanics E_sub -> F-actin -> LATS1/2 -> Y_nuc phosphorylation kinetics (Dupont et al. 2011) alongside intercellular Dll1-Notch phase coupling." ;
    pk:hasScore 9.15e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-hubaud-yap-excitable-segmentation-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
